@startuml seq-git-open-diff
'' ============================================================================
'' vinary-viewer — Sequence: a commit diff, from row click to rev-aware Split
'' (ADR-0039 D4/D6). PlantUML over Mermaid because the DISTINGUISHING moves are
'' seam crossings: main verifies and spills but only returns a PATH; the
'' renderer owns navigation; and the ordinary diff pipeline then re-crosses the
'' seam for blob-exact enrichment — three round trips one flowchart would blur.
'' ============================================================================
!include _vv-theme.iuml

title Commit diff — verify → git diff → spill → navigate → rev-aware enrichment

autonumber "0:"

actor User #white
participant "ui.commits row /\npill / range input" as Panel RENDERER_TINT
participant "re-frame\nevents / fx" as RF REFRAME_TINT
participant "renderer\n(diff view)" as Rend RENDERER_TINT
participant "preload `window.vv`" as Vv IPC_TINT
participant "main.service\n(open! / diff sources)" as Svc MAIN_TINT
participant "main.git\n(handle-open-diff)" as Git MAIN_TINT
participant "git CLI" as CLI FS_TINT
participant "spill + doc-overrides\n($XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/…/git-diff)" as Spill FS_TINT

== choose the pair ==
alt row click (diff vs FIRST parent)
  User -> Panel : click a commit row
  Panel -> RF : `[:commits/select … :single]`\n+ `[:commits/activate root hash]`
  RF -> Vv : `gitOpenDiff {root, to hash,\nparent? true}` **vv:git-open-diff**
else two selected → "Diff selected"
  User -> Panel : Ctrl+click ×2 → pill
  Panel -> RF : `[:commits/diff-selected root]`\n(`diff-pair` orders older→newer)
  RF -> Vv : `gitOpenDiff {root, from, to}`
else free-form range
  User -> Panel : type `HEAD~3..HEAD` ⏎
  Panel -> RF : `[:commits/range-submit]` →\n`parse-range` (`A..B` / `A...B` /\nsingle-rev-vs-parent)
  RF -> Vv : `gitOpenDiff {root, from, to, dots?}`
end

== verify + diff + spill (main) ==
Vv -> Git : `handle-open-diff`
Git -> CLI : `rev-parse --verify --quiet\n--end-of-options <to>^{commit}`
CLI --> Git : full sha (else the inline error\n"unknown revision: …")
alt from given (pill / range)
  Git -> CLI : verify `<from>` the same way\n(a typo is the user's input)
else parent-of-to
  Git -> CLI : verify `<to-sha>^`
  CLI --> Git : sha — or FAILS for a **root commit**
  Git -> Git : from ← the **empty tree**\n`4b825dc…904` (R4: one plain\n`git diff`, no `git show` arm)
end
alt [root from to] already spilled (dedupe hit)
  Git --> Vv : {path existing, title}
else fresh pair
  Git -> CLI : `git diff --no-color\n**--no-ext-diff** --end-of-options\n<from> <to>`\n(repo config must never pick\nan external diff *program*)
  CLI --> Git : diff text (≤ 64 MiB)
  Git -> Spill : write `<uuid>/<shortA..shortB>.diff`\n(dir 0700, file 0600)
  Git -> Spill : doc-overrides `register!`\n{kind "diff", **stdin? true**, cwd root,\n**git {root from to range?}**}
  Git --> Vv : {path, title}
end
Vv --> RF : reply — a PATH, never a tab:\nnavigation is renderer-owned

== the ordinary diff pipeline (feature 28, unchanged) ==
RF -> RF : `[:tab/navigate path]`\n(history, retention, facets)
RF -> Vv : **vv:open** path
Vv -> Svc : `open!` — effective kind "diff"\n(:stdin? → MRU-excluded, unwatched;\n:git → **no** tree adoption, ADR-0038 R7)
Svc --> Vv : **vv:content** {kind "diff",\nbaseDir = repo root}
Vv --> RF : `[:content/received]` → `:diff/render`
RF -> Rend : unified render; Split on demand
Rend -> Vv : **vv:load-diff-sources**\n{diffPath, files, includePaths,\nincludeContent?}
Vv -> Svc : handler: `doc-overrides/git-info`\npresent → the **rev-aware** arm (R8)
Svc -> Git : `load-rev-sources {root to} rels`
Git -> CLI : `cat-file blob <to>:<rel>` per file\n(plumbing: no textconv, no filters)
CLI --> Git : blob content **as of <to>** —\nexact Split alignment even when\nthe working tree has drifted
Git -> Svc : targets still resolve against the\n**working tree** (a header click\nmeans "open this file NOW")
Svc --> Vv : {rel → {path?, content?}}
Vv --> Rend : enriched sources
Rend --> User : unified + blob-exact Split;\nmissing blob → hunk-window fallback

== release ==
User -> RF : close the tab
RF -> Vv : retention sync\n(**vv:retained-files**)
Vv -> Svc : `unwatch-file!` → unlink the spill\n+ `git/forget-spill!` (dedupe entry)
note right of Spill #FFF6D6
  Crashed sessions: a boot-time
  `git/sweep-stale!` (10-min age gate,
  the stdin sweep's twin) clears
  abandoned spill dirs.
end note

legend right
  |= Colour |= Concept |
  |<#2D9574>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| Renderer / UI |
  |<#4F97D7>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| re-frame events / fx |
  |<#B1951D>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| IPC seam |
  |<#3A5BA0>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| MAIN (service + vinary.main.git) |
  |<#9F8766>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| git CLI / spill files |
endlegend
@enduml
